  "Desktop.UnexpectedTrayCommand": "Unexpected tray menu command: {0}.",
  "Desktop.UnsupportedStartupValueKind": "Startup registry value kind {0} cannot be restored safely.",
  "Firmware.Guide.Failure": "5. If an error occurs, do not try to install an arbitrary firmware file. Consult the manufacturer’s instructions and support. This guide does not confirm the safety of an independent Windows updater.",
  "Firmware.Guide.KeepConnected": "4. Follow only the steps shown by the manufacturer’s application. Do not disconnect the receiver during the update. The device restarts after a successful update.",
  "Firmware.Guide.ReadManual": "2. Open the official LARK A1 manual and check the current manufacturer requirements. The supplied English document describes updating on page 12.",
  "Firmware.Guide.Reconnect": "6. After finishing in the manufacturer’s application, plug the receiver back into a Windows USB port. Hollylark reads the only detected receiver automatically; if several are detected, choose the receiver in the list to read its versions.",
  "Firmware.Guide.RecordVersions": "1. Record the RX and transmitter versions read from the device. A version number alone does not confirm that an update is available or compatible.",
  "Firmware.Guide.UseOfficialApplication": "3. Stop using the receiver in Hollylark. Perform the update in the manufacturer’s application on a compatible mobile device, with the transmitters connected to the receiver. HollyAudio is the current name of the application previously described as LarkSound.",
  "Firmware.GuideLabel": "_Guide to updating LARK A1 in the manufacturer’s application:",
  "Firmware.GuideName": "Guide to updating LARK A1 in the manufacturer’s application",
  "Firmware.NoVersion": "No current version reading. Plug in the USB receiver, select it in the list if several are detected, and use F5 in the main window to read or retry.",
  "Firmware.PageName": "Firmware versions and update guide",
  "Firmware.ScrollName": "Firmware information and guide",
  "Firmware.SummaryLabel": "Receiver and microphone firmware _versions read from the device:",
  "Firmware.SummaryName": "Receiver and microphone firmware versions read from the device",
  "Firmware.Title": "Hollylark — firmware and manufacturer support",
  "Firmware.Warning": "This window is a guide, not an updater. Hollylark does not download or write firmware, switch the device to update mode or check whether the version read is the latest. Opening this window and copying the addresses below does not send commands to the receiver.",
  "Firmware.WarningLabel": "Important _limitation: Hollylark does not update firmware",
  "Firmware.WarningName": "Important limitation: Hollylark does not update firmware",
  "Help.Guide.ApplyChanges": "3. By default, changes require the Apply button. In Settings, you can enable automatic application of new selections after a short pause; slider movements are combined into one change when released. Success always requires a response and a matching device readback. An existing draft is not sent automatically when the mode changes. Changing the selected microphone or group discards unsent drafts and cancels queued automatic changes. Changes to active microphone connections also discard unsent drafts and cancel queued automatic changes without changing the selected microphone or group. Individual mute is addressed by microphone index. All microphones sends mute or unmute commands to connected microphones sequentially; the operation is not atomic, and a failure or group membership change may leave some changes applied.",
  "Help.Guide.AudioMeter": "The audio meter requires explicitly selecting a Windows audio input and starting measurement. It does not automatically use the default microphone, save recordings or send audio over the network. Measuring a Windows input is not a level reading through the USB control protocol. You can record in a separate audio application.",
  "Help.Guide.Battery": "Microphone battery levels are read only for connected transmitters. No connection does not mean 0% battery. The protocol identified for LARK A1 does not expose the case battery or charging status; check the indicator on the case.",
  "Help.Guide.Cancellation": "Cancel at the bottom of the window stops waiting for the current operation. Unplugging the receiver or selecting another receiver, microphone or group also interrupts reading or applying settings. Use F5 to read or retry the selected receiver. Cancellation does not undo a command already sent to the device. An error or timeout means no confirmation, not certainty that the device is unchanged.",
  "Help.Guide.Connection": "1. Connect the LARK A1 USB-C receiver using a data-capable cable or adapter. The charging case is not a receiver. Turn on the transmitters.",
  "Help.Guide.DesktopIntegration": "Autostart is an optional Windows entry for the current user and does not require an administrator. The tray is also optional. Win+B opens the notification area; the icon menu includes restore, settings, read, gain adjustment, mute for each available TX and Exit. Gain changes follow the selected microphone or group and the same shared-parameter restrictions; mute entries address their named microphone by index. Audio commands apply the change immediately and verify the readback. If the window was hidden, they restore it to show an accessible result. Exit actually closes the application.",
  "Help.Guide.Diagnostics": "Help → Information and diagnostics also includes Read SN and MAC for the receiver and connected TX units. No response reports an error, not an invented value. Saved diagnostics go to reports beside the application; they may include the device path, firmware, serial numbers, MAC addresses and USB reports — share them knowingly. The application sends no telemetry.",
  "Help.Guide.Firmware": "The application does not update firmware, reset or pair transmitters. The firmware window shows versions read from the device and a guide; it is not an updater and does not check for a new version. The Lightning variant is not supported.",
  "Help.Guide.FirstRun": "First launch: before the main window opens, select a theme and the other presentation options, then choose Continue. Escape does not close the wizard or application; it can dismiss an open dropdown. Cancel or Alt+F4 exits without saving or opening the main window. The setup wizard returns until completed; existing settings and profiles are preserved. A settings read error stops startup instead of replacing them with a new configuration. The theme is applied only after Continue, so screen reader list navigation is not interrupted.",
  "Help.Guide.Introduction": "Hollylark — an independent application for controlling LARK A1 over USB. It is not an official Hollyland application.",
  "Help.Guide.Keyboard": "Keyboard: Tab and Shift+Tab — controls; Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+Shift+Tab — tabs; arrow keys — lists, including receiver and microphone or group selection; Enter or Space — buttons; Alt — menu; F5 — read or retry; Alt+F4 — close. Escape closes auxiliary windows or cancels application settings.",
  "Help.Guide.Language": "Changing the language in Settings is saved when you choose OK and takes effect on the next launch. Until then, the interface remains in its current language. Cancel discards the unsaved selection.",
  "Help.Guide.MicrophoneSelection": "Microphones: use the arrow keys in the native list of physical microphones 1 to N and All microphones. Tab visits the action button for the selected item only. Individual item names include connection, mute and battery status; All microphones shows the connected count and mute state, never a battery. All microphones requires at least two active, connected microphones; if only one is active, select it. On the first status read, the sole connected microphone is selected if there is exactly one; otherwise, All microphones is selected. Later joins or departures do not automatically change this selection. In the known protocol, gain, noise cancellation, EQ, reverb, channel mode and other device parameters are shared, not independently addressed. With several active microphones, an individual target offers only mute or unmute; select All microphones for shared parameters. With one active microphone, you can edit shared parameters under that microphone, but they remain receiver-wide and may affect transmitters that reconnect later.",
  "Help.Guide.Profiles": "An audio profile reads fresh gain, channel, noise reduction, EQ and reverb values before creation. It does not include muting, batteries, pairing or firmware. The name and profile list are part of the settings draft. Apply profile is a separate, explicit device operation; Cancel in Settings does not undo it. A USB failure can leave some changes applied. A profile does not automatically unmute microphones to change noise reduction. Profiles contain shared receiver settings, not independent per-microphone presets. Applying a profile follows the selected microphone or group: with several active microphones, select All microphones; with one, select that microphone. Even then, settings remain receiver-wide and may affect transmitters that reconnect later.",
  "Help.Guide.ReceiverSelection": "2. USB receivers are detected automatically. The only detected receiver becomes active and its status is read, including when it is already plugged in at startup. If several are detected, choose one with the arrow keys in the single receiver list. There is no fixed receiver-count limit. Physically unplugging the active receiver ends its session. Automatic reading does not apply a profile or write audio settings. Automatic setting writes occur only if you explicitly enabled automatic application of new selections in Controls.",
  "Help.Guide.Refresh": "4. Automatic reads every 2 seconds do not overwrite unapplied selections. Read or retry (F5) discards those selections and reads the state again, including after a read failure. Unplugging the active receiver or selecting another also discards unapplied selections; they are not sent to the newly selected receiver.",
  "Help.Guide.SafetyGates": "Every device setting change, including LEDs and automatic power-off, requires at least one connected microphone. Status is checked again before sending each command. Muting requires a connected microphone and receiver firmware read as at least 1.0.1.3. Identification requires the corresponding report field and two connected microphones; in a recognised four-TX mode, one is enough. Noise reduction is blocked when all connected microphones are muted. Automatic power-off after 15 minutes applies to being unpaired, not to silence. Gain has six levels, without unverified dB values.",
  "Help.Guide.SavingSettings": "OK or Enter saves settings and closes the window without another question. Escape, Cancel or closing a window with unsaved changes asks whether to save: Yes saves and closes; No discards changes and closes. A save error keeps the window open. Settings are stored in data/settings.json beside the application. Resetting a category changes only the draft, not the device. Exit confirmation is enabled by default; previously saved choices remain unchanged. Disabling hints or action messages does not hide errors or warnings. Routine battery polling does not repeat announcements.",
  "Help.Guide.Settings": "Program → Settings opens Appearance, Main screen, Controls, Startup and closing, and Audio profiles. Available themes are Light and Dark. Rows can be hidden and gain adjusted with a list, buttons or slider. Current value display: Read-only fields shows confirmed values in edit fields, Text shows them as text, and No additional values removes the extra readings, including the gain draft reading. The list or slider’s own value remains available. Fields do not contain explanations. Connection status, errors and warnings remain available. Turning hints off removes optional headings and guidance, including screen reader hints. After enabling automatic application, subsequent control selections may send commands to the receiver; saving application settings alone never sends earlier drafts.",
  "Help.Guide.SupportLinks": "The buttons below the instructions copy the official address of the English LARK A1 manual or the HollyAudio Google Play listing published by Hollyland to the clipboard. Paste the copied address into a browser. The buttons do not open websites or install applications or firmware.",
