  "Settings.Retention.Label": "_Preserve volatile microphone settings",
  "Retention.Restoring": "Restoring remembered parameters after microphones reconnected.",
  "Retention.Restored": "Device readback confirmed the restored parameters.",
  "Retention.Interrupted": "Not all parameters were restored. Device state or microphone connections changed during the operation. Review current values; this operation will not be retried in a loop.",
  "Retention.StoreError": "Cannot safely read or save remembered parameters in {0}. Automatic restoration is suspended. Check the file and permissions.",
  "Help.Guide.GlobalHotkeys": "Global shortcuts: open Settings, Keyboard shortcuts. Select an action with the arrows, then Tab to the editable field and Capture shortcut. An empty field removes a binding. Escape cancels capture without closing Settings. Enable shortcuts and save with OK; disabling keeps bindings. They are disabled by default and suspended in Settings. They work while Hollylark is running, including in the background, with microphone/group restrictions and confirmed readback. A global read refuses when unsent choices exist; ordinary F5 discards them. Resetting defaults disables shortcuts again.",
  "Help.Guide.StateAnnouncements": "State announcements: Announce device state changes through the screen reader also covers confirmed changes made through a phone or microphone buttons. Prism sends these messages directly to a running screen reader, including while another application is active or Hollylark is minimized or hidden in the tray. Keep prism.dll beside Hollylark.exe. NVDA is preferred when several supported readers are running. No standalone Windows voice is started. If direct delivery is unavailable or fails, Hollylark falls back to UI Automation notifications, whose presentation depends on the reader. A successful direct request does not also send the same UI Automation notification. Messages do not move focus or interrupt current reader speech. Unchanged state and battery fluctuations remain silent. Disabling this option stops routine device-state announcements, not important errors. Readers must run in the same Windows session and desktop; speech heard by a person still requires manual verification.",
  "Help.Guide.Retention": "Preserve volatile settings is enabled by default. Confirmed shared parameters are remembered per receiver USB path in data/retained-settings.json next to the executable. External changes during a continuous connection become the new baseline. After an observed disconnection and return, differing parameters of the whole active group are restored with fresh checks and readback. Mute is not restored and microphones are never automatically unmuted. If the first device snapshot already has active microphones, their current state is adopted without writing an old configuration; if they are first observed disconnected, remembered values may return when they connect. Another USB path does not inherit settings. Cycles entirely between polls or while the program is closed cannot be reliably identified. Unavailable changes are not forced by unmuting or bypassing microphone-count gates. Errors or concurrent changes stop the attempt without looping. Open Settings and unsent drafts prevent starting restoration. F5 and identity reads stay read-only; deferred restoration may occur on a later background poll."
}
